RED BUILD: the hooks (objserv.cxx, sfxbasemodel.cxx, autorecovery.cxx, the .uno:HstAutoSave slot) are left out, so CppunitTest_sfx2_hst_autosave must fail.

HST Office: AutoSave into the document's own file, decided per document, never with a dialog (owner decision
21/11/2026).

Upstream UserAutoSave (Recovery/AutoSave/UserAutoSaveEnabled) calls XStorable::store() on every document of the
process: it overwrites .doc, .txt, .csv or .rtf files silently in their lossy format, drops macros a .docx cannot
hold and lets SfxMedium::CheckFileDate ask "the file was changed by another program" in the middle of typing.
With this patch the AutoRecovery timer (3 minutes, 10 for large files, after 10 s without input) asks each
document whether it stores itself now, and the document then stores itself without any question:

- sfx2 hstuserautosave.{hxx,cxx} (new, HST): per-document state in SfxObjectShell_Impl, for the session only;
  every opened document starts with UserAutoSaveEnabled. A document stores itself only when it has a file: URL
  (local, network or USB drive), is in ODF or MS Word/Excel/PowerPoint 2007 XML (.docx/.xlsx/.pptx), is not read
  only, hidden or embedded, has no digital signature and no macros the format drops (the test of
  hst-macro-save-guard.patch, through hst::autosave::FormatKeepsMacros in guisaveas.cxx), and AutoRecovery is on.
  An administrator lock of UserAutoSaveEnabled (or AutoSave/Enabled) is shown as it is set. A Calc cell edit in
  progress (ScDocShell::HstIsInputActive) or a modal dialog skips the round.
- slot .uno:HstAutoSave (SID_HST_AUTOSAVE, SfxObjectShell ExecFile_Impl/GetState_Impl): checked while the
  document saves itself, disabled when it cannot; executing it switches the document (a paused one runs again).
- SfxBaseModel::getArgs2 answers HstUserAutoSave (store now) and HstUserAutoSaving (inside such a store, for the
  "Phiên bản trước" job) only when asked for by name; getArgs() is unchanged.
- SfxBaseModel::storeSelf accepts HstUserAutoSave: the document is checked again and stored with a silent
  interaction handler (warnings approved, every question aborted), so a file changed by another program is not
  overwritten. A failed store pauses AutoSave of the document ("Tạm dừng": write error, or changed by another
  program); a save by the user (storeSelf, storeAsURL) ends the pause.
- framework autorecovery.cxx: the in-place store is the document's decision (getArgs2) and goes through
  storeSelf({HstUserAutoSave}); session saves still need the global flag, so HST session restart and session end
  never store originals. After an in-place store the empty file reserved for a recovery copy is removed and the
  document's next change waits the whole interval (the 30 s first-copy rule is for documents without a copy).
- strings (EN in sfx2 strings.hrc, VI in messages.po) of the toggle and its tooltips; the command label in
  GenericCommands.xcu.

License: the new HST files are HST-owned (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary); the upstream files remain under their
original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: make CppunitTest_sfx2_hst_autosave (hst-user-autosave-test.patch); tests/unit/test_user_autosave_patch.py.
